 "notes": "Koh Haa Yai (Koh Haa No. 5), the largest of the Koh Haa islets; island outlines from OpenStreetMap. The Cathedral caverns on its southern shore, the swim-through, boulders and depths, on the OSM coastline (positions are approximate); the chambers open from low-tide level to 14 m, the first two are joined by a swim-through at about 9 m and the largest has an air space under stalactites (Phuket Dive Guide). The Chimney that the site description mentions is at Koh Haa No. 1 according to Phuket Dive Guide and is not drawn and the Lagoon between islands 2-4, 700 m to the north-east, is a separate dive and left off. The site coordinates (7.45, 98.98) are 10 km east of the islands; the origin here is on Koh Haa Yai.",
